hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1076","Our father told me, on the authority of Aisha. H Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to pray thirteen rak’ahs at night. He would perform the Witr prayer with five prostrations, meaning rak’ahs, without saying the salaam during them, so he would sit in the afterlife, then “He says the salaam.” This is the hadith of Abu Usama, and Bundar said: He says the Witr prayer with five of them, and he does not say the salaam except in the last of them."
